chisel
Usage: chisel server -p PORT --reverse   |   chisel client OP:PORT R:socks

A tcp/udp tunnel that rides over http, for pivoting through a firewall that
only lets http out. Run the server on your own box; the client on the foothold
dials back and opens a socks proxy you route the rest of your tools through.

	server -p PORT --reverse    operator side: accept reverse tunnels
	client OP:PORT R:socks      foothold side: reverse socks proxy
	client OP:PORT L:9000:host:445   forward a single local port

For authorised engagements only; a tunnel through someone else's firewall is
exactly what you must have permission for.

See also: socat, ligolo-proxy, ligolo-agent
